{
	"_doc": "Set pieces: authored layout recipes for famous Night City places (SetPieces, SetPieceGen). The book gives no floor plans, so a set piece is a recipe the generators follow: the place stays recognisable while the rooms vary per seed. Keys: name; locations {location id (data/world/locations.json): params that location adds, e.g. which structure is the target}; faction (the Security Code's faction, the default opposition); base {scene (scenes.json; its theme, doctrine and civilians), planner (SetPieceGen: plot = a building plot with its annexes, port = quays and anchored ships)}; params (scene params; the caller's win); plot (the building plot: margin, front yard depth, fence along the street, yard kind and ground, annexes behind or beside the main building); sites {part: {base: a sites.json site, then site keys that replace the base's (layout replaces key by key)}}: part main is the target building unless locations say otherwise; posts [{where: roof | deck | room:<kind>, part, kind, count [a, b], weapon (the guard posted there carries it as their primary), cover (sandbags round the post)}]: posts the guards man first; props [{where, part, piece, count}]; key_rooms {part (or _scene: the outdoor rooms): [room kinds every seed must have]}; anchors {objective kind: {room kind: score}} (a site part may carry its own; Encounter.secure_cell, which only reaches rooms without a locked security door, so anchors name staff-zone rooms; data uses the NET instead, eliminate needs no anchor); rules (special rules the engine honours: public_access, civilians); todo (rules the engine can't honour yet); look (tags for the view; the walls and windows themselves come from the site keys); cite; _why: which book detail each element follows and what is ours. Program keys only set pieces use (Layouts.program): keep {floor: {bands: [first, last]} | {u: [from, to]}} keeps only those bands (or that share of the facade) on a storey, so upper floors step back and the roofs below become terraces; secret {group: note}: items tagged secret: group are built on one floor only, drawn per seed; mirror: false fixes the plan's handedness.",

