		"_why": "Book (NC2045 p.153-154, Port of Night City #5 Flotsam and #7 Main Port; both Security Code 10 Thelas Marines Hardened Heavy). Main Port as printed: Quay 1 hand-offloaded (pallets and crates, no cranes), Quays 2 and 3 for bulk cargo with two container cranes each and rail to the Yard (four cranes, a rail strip, the container yard, the freighter moored there), Quay 4 the newest with cranes plus a dedicated hangar and control facility for cargo drones (drone_hangar with its control room), Quay 5 about half built (a construction site at the end of the quay). Flotsam as printed: small ships, kelongs, pontoon docks and floats anchored to three wrecks in the bay: the OGV Lund (a war-adrift container ship, under 2,000 of its 5,000 containers salvaged: a decayed hulk with containers on deck), the Rose (an old submarine, the heart of Thelas communications run by Netrunners, home of the tug pilots' club: comms_room, server_room, the Pilots' Club bar) and the Sakata Maru (once an Arasaka munitions and transport ship, now the Port's administration centre with Calypso's office and senior management, retrofitted with anti-aircraft weapons: the admin superstructure with bullpen, offices and Calypso's exec_office, the bridge above, the old magazines kept as armories, AA gun mounts on the open deck). The Main Port location targets the freighter, Flotsam the Sakata Maru. Ours: one map for both (Flotsam lies in the bay off the quays, joined to the port by a long float walkway), the quay order west to east, the bow taper, the superstructure aft, the kelongs' positions and the fenced port gate on the road."
